<http://data.silknow.org/object/cf112789-ef0e-3375-9a2c-8c91b9df71ca/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Forehead band, part of a Norwegian bridal costume purchased by the donor in 1865 from the original owner. The piece consists of two parts: a rounded length of red worsted fabric with three rows of applied silver lace, and silk rosettes decorated with coloured glass beads; and a narrow brocaded silk ribbon stitched to the reverse, such that the pleated pink silk trim is visible from the front. \n\nTo the reverse, a patchwork of printed floral cottons line the main body of the band. Two pairs of tying strings of green woollen braid are attached at each end. \n\nWorn as part of a larger headdress assemblage known as <i>lad</i>, traditionally topped with a bridal crown."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cf112789-ef0e-3375-9a2c-8c91b9df71ca> .

